  "body": "Fixed on \\`main\\` in b8a7eea8 (`fix(world): keep a relocated grant covering its own source`).\n\nConfirmed and reproduced: running from a directory granted with \\`{ path = \"/tmp/proj\", at = \"/workspace\" }\\` gave \\`PWD=/home/<user>\\` plus the \"working directory is not granted\" warning; after the fix the same run gives \\`PWD=/workspace\\` and the project files list, while an ungranted cwd still falls back to the private home as before.\n\nRoot cause: not the \\`at\\` feature itself (e8db2d8 kept \\`covered_by_grant\\` matching \\`rule.path\\`). The regression came from a0838487 (`fix(world): a relocated grant keeps the private /tmp`), which correctly taught \\`policy_touches\\` to match \\`rule.at\\` for its sandbox-side question (\"does a grant land in /tmp?\"), but applied the same swap to \\`covered_by_grant\\`. Those two ask from opposite ends: \\`covered_by_grant\\` is only ever passed host paths (real home, invocation dir, \\`XDG_RUNTIME_DIR\\`, \\`/tmp/.X11-unix\\`) and must match the grant source. Matching only the placement dropped the cwd.\n\nFix matches a host path against both the source and the placement, per your suggested patch, so the cwd is restored and a grant relocated onto e.g. the real home or the X11 socket is still recognized. Added a regression test.\n\nOn the version question: no errand change is needed. Deployed bailey 0.1.1 predates relocated grants, so it is unaffected and errand works on it today; the break only appears on 0.1.2+. Once this lands in a release, errand can adopt it and pick up the btrfs-ioctl fix.",
